# Every text file is checked out with LF, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which checks text out with
# CRLF -- and Prettier, whose endOfLine is "lf", then reads every file in ui/src
# as misformatted: `npm run format:check` failed on all of them on a clean clone,
# and `npm run format` "fixed" that by rewriting files nobody had touched. CI never
# saw it, the runners checking out LF. .claude/hooks/session-start.sh is the same
# mistake a shell over: a CRLF shebang line names an interpreter that is not there.
# Saying it here makes the checkout the same on every machine rather than on every
# machine configured like the runners.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The four kinds of file here that are not text, said so rather than guessed at.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.mpg binary
*.wav binary
